(1) 1134/    6514 :                     ScrollHoriz:
(1) 1151/    6514 :                     		; The intent of this code is to make the camera briefly lag behind the
(1) 1152/    6514 :                     		; player right after releasing a spin dash, however it does this by
(1) 1153/    6514 :                     		; simply making the camera use position data from previous frames. This
(1) 1154/    6514 :                     		; means that if the camera had been moving recently enough, then
(1) 1155/    6514 :                     		; releasing a spin dash will cause the camera to jerk around instead of
(1) 1156/    6514 :                     		; remain still. This can be encountered by running into a wall, and
(1) 1157/    6514 :                     		; quickly turning around and spin dashing away. Sonic 3 would have had
(1) 1158/    6514 :                     		; this same issue with the Fire Shield's dash abiliity, but it shoddily
(1) 1159/    6514 :                     		; works around the issue by resetting the old position values to the
(1) 1160/    6514 :                     		; current position (see 'Reset_Player_Position_Array').
(1) 1161/    6514 : 3215                		move.w	Horiz_scroll_delay_val-Camera_Delay(a5),d1	; should scrolling be delayed?
(1) 1162/    6516 : 671E                		beq.s	.scrollNotDelayed				; if not, branch
(1) 1163/    6518 : 0441 0100           		subi.w	#$100,d1					; reduce delay value
(1) 1164/    651C : 3A81                		move.w	d1,Horiz_scroll_delay_val-Camera_Delay(a5)
(1) 1165/    651E : 7200                		moveq	#0,d1
