    4408/    72F6 :                     		; What follows is a very C style compare code for zones that aren't GHZ, LZ, or EndZ.
    4409/    72F6 :                     		; This works well in-game, except for LZ which uses the same data as CPZ.
    4410/    72F6 :                     		; What this could point to is that at some point, LZ used compressed chunks similar to that of GHZ.
    4411/    72F6 :                     		; However, instead it tries to decompress chunks that are already uncompressed to begin with.
    4412/    72F6 :                     
    4413/    72F6 :                     		; This could also be entirely rewritten so that EndZ is compared first, and if equal, then branch to the decompression routine.
    4414/    72F6 :                     		; Then it could follow up with a check to see if the zone is greater than or equal to CPZ, simplifying the following compares into
    4415/    72F6 :                     		; just two compares.
    4416/    72F6 :                     
