(2)  183/   754BA :                     	; These first three notes are too high when combined with this track's
(2)  184/   754BA :                     	; transposition value, causing them to overflow the PSG frequency table
(2)  185/   754BA :                     	; and play invalid notes. In the Sonic 1 prototype, this problem was
(2)  186/   754BA :                     	; even worse as there were smpsChangeTransposition commands around the
(2)  187/   754BA :                     	; following line that raised the notes yet another octave higher,
(2)  188/   754BA :                     	; causing the fourth note to break too.
(2)  189/   754BA :                     	; Since the commands are gone now, we can assume that this was the
(2)  190/   754BA :                     	; developers' intended solution, though it unfortunately only fixed the
(2)  191/   754BA :                     	; fourth note. So, in order to fix the bug for good, the notes on the
(2)  192/   754BA :                     	; following line have to be lowered by yet another octave.
(2)  193/   754BA : 8006 C103 0306      	dc.b	nRst, $06, nE5, $03, $03, $06, nRst, nE4, $24
            754C0 : 80B5 24          
